18:'Review convergence evidence and explain any remaining anomaly, missing evidence, contradiction, ambiguity, defect, or variance. The application calculates mandatory requirement coverage, verification coverage, regression success, defect counts, unresolved unknowns, contradiction/ambiguity counts, unexplained variance, and the final convergence result from current canonical records. Do not set or override those application-derived values.',
19:'After convergence, perform only the declared unchanged-confirmation operations using the exact application-supplied converged component versions and hashes with zero material changes. Use the supplied new run/context identities, rerun the complete verification matrix and applicable regression suite across ten new independent contexts, compare all runs, and report any new defect, missed requirement, missed failure case, or correctness-affecting variance. The application evaluates unchanged-confirmation completion and owns iteration/run/context identity.',
20:'Inspect the proposed production baseline only after successful unchanged confirmation. The human authorizes the baseline and the application assigns BASELINE_ID, freezes exact approved versions and artifact bytes, calculates hashes, and records immutable baseline identity. Report substantive discrepancies or blockers only; do not assign baseline identity, hashes, authorization, or lifecycle state.',
21:'Produce the job’s approved deliverable only when the actual authorized execution environment can do so reliably from the approved baseline. Generate the complete approved deliverable and every required actual artifact whenever this environment can reliably construct the artifact bytes from the accepted specification, documented representation, and sufficient inputs. Do not require possession of a downstream authoring or consuming application merely to generate a source, interchange, drawing, document, data, model, or machine-readable artifact whose representation can be constructed correctly here. Treat compilation, import/open validation, simulation, post-processing, machine execution, fabrication, deployment, filing/submission, and physical testing as separate downstream operations: claim them only when they actually occurred in a capable authorized environment with evidence. Use an implementation-ready or manufacturing-ready specification/patch plan only when the approved artifact itself cannot be generated reliably here; otherwise produce the real artifact and separately preserve any downstream verification still required. The application assigns PRODUCT_ID and execution identity and is authoritative for persisted file bytes, filenames, media types, sizes, hashes, storage references, and lineage.',
22:'Perform the substantive deterministic verification work that is actually supported against the finished product and report procedures, expected results, actual observed results, evidence, and defects. Use specialized deterministic tools when the authorized execution context provides them. Objective artifact identities, byte sizes, cryptographic hashes, expected test-set completeness, counts, and final gate calculations are application-owned. Never claim an unexecuted deterministic check ran.',
