24:'Perform adversarial verification on the finished product. Test applicable missing material, prohibited material, contradictions, impossible logic, unsupported facts, external-source misrepresentation, wrong versions, broken references, hidden assumptions, partial completion, nonsensical meaning, terminology inconsistency, unhandled exceptions, stale facts, malformed files, hidden content, export corruption, superficial keyword compliance, historical regressions, and domain-specific failure modes. Preserve attack, method, expected behavior, actual result, defect, severity, and evidence. Do not claim attacks that were not actually executed.',
25:'Inspect the exact final delivered representation and package. Report substantive rendering/opening observations, clipping, missing or blank content, broken layout, graphics, font substitution, overlap, hidden content, ordering, export corruption, package problems, defects, and irreducible human/reviewer judgments. For drawings, CAD/CAM, CNC, and additive-manufacturing artifacts, inspect every required view/representation and verify that human-visible units, scales, datums/coordinates, dimensions/tolerances, notes, revision identifiers, and manufacturing information are present and coherent where applicable. The application derives canonical artifact inventory, filenames, byte sizes, SHA-256 values, and other objective file facts from actual stored bytes.',
26:'Reconcile this job’s process evidence and product evidence as two separate propositions. Report substantive discrepancies, unauthorized-modification evidence, chain-of-custody issues, defects, blockers, and review findings. The application calculates canonical counts, identities, completeness, and gate state. Neither process correctness nor product correctness proves the other.',
27:'Review the current release evidence for substantive gaps, contradictions, unsupported findings, unresolved defects, blockers, or evidence problems. Do not set a release state. The application evaluates the complete current evidence and creates exactly one idempotent ACCEPTED, REJECTED, or BLOCKED release determination. Human or agent preference cannot override that deterministic result, and ACCEPTED does not itself authorize delivery.',
